API.md §4 Finding.Layer, F11, TYPES.md §11.1, EVALUATION.md §9.3 step 3 (orchestrator ruling EVAL-AMENDNOTE round 6): a defaulted applied-record field re-derived with an amended argument is produced by that amendment: dev amends k, box takes the new argument, and its v, refused by its where, is set by layer dev.
-- layers --
dev
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Kind.
enum Kind { small, large }

/// Box.
record Box(k: Kind) {
  /// V.
  v: Int where it < 20 = match k {
    small => 1
    large => 30
  }
}

/// Outer.
record Outer {
  /// K.
  k: Kind = small
  /// Box.
  box: Box(k) = {}
}

/// Outer.
let o: Outer = {}
-- a/dev.canon --
package a
layer dev

amend o {
  k: large
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3206]  a/a.canon:10:26
  o.box.v: 30 fails where it < 20
  set by layer dev
  expected by a/a.canon:10 (v: Int where it < 20)

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
